alphabet a b

# Language: b+ (the last symbol is b and no a occurs before it).
# Nonempty -- "b" and "bb" are members, checked with --word.
#
# The one-variable route calls this EMPTY:
#   java -jar JAR this.brasp --run-native                  -> sat, witness "b"   (correct)
#   java -jar JAR this.brasp --run-abc                     -> NOT PROVED         (correct)
#   java -jar JAR this.brasp --one-variable --run-native   -> unsat, "empty"     (WRONG)
#
# The trigger is a negated attention conjoined with another condition:
# `!seen_a` alone is answered correctly, `is_b & !seen_a` is not.
is_a = symbol a
is_b = symbol b
seen_a = rightmost(is_a@j, true)
accept = is_b & !seen_a

output accept
